# Timer slots captured after setting three timers at 03:07, 11:22 and 19:45,
# Glowrium-C045, 2026-07-28.
#
# The app fills slots in order, so only the THIRD timer landed in a readable
# slot. GTimeDat0 (key 4) and GTimeDat1 (key 40) hold 03:07 and 11:22 and are
# never returned by a read.
#
# GTimeDat2 (key 41) holds 19:45. Byte 1 = 19 and byte 2 = 45 decode the time
# exactly, which is what identifies the layout. GTimeDat3/4 are empty and give
# the baseline to diff against.
#
# Only the 12-byte config prefix is stored here; the 100-byte DyData program
# that follows it is covered by other fixtures.
slot2_enabled_1945: 80 13 2d 01 64 64 08 1e 00 00 80 00
slot3_empty: 00 00 1e 00 64 64 08 1e 00 00 00 00
slot4_empty: 00 00 1e 00 64 64 08 1e 00 00 00 00
#
# Follow-up 1: the 19:45 timer was changed to repeat=daily, action=off.
#   byte 0:  0x80 -> 0xff    enable bit plus a WEEKDAY BITMASK.
#                            once = 0x80 (enabled, no days)
#                            daily = 0xff (enabled, all seven bits)
#   byte 3:  1 -> 0          action: 1 = on, 0 = off
#   byte 5:  100 -> 101      unexplained
#   byte 10 stayed 0x80, so it is NOT the repeat rule.
#
# Byte 0 packs the enable bit together with a weekday bitmask.
slot2_daily_off: ff 13 2d 00 64 65 08 1e 00 00 80 00
#
# Follow-up 2: a timer built entirely in Python and written to slot 2,
# 06:53, weekdays only (0x1f), action on. Read back byte-for-byte.
slot2_written_0653_weekdays: 9f 06 35 01 64 65 08 1e 00 00 80 00
